<%!-- The one page the service worker is allowed to keep (issue #1729), shown
instead of the browser's own offline error.

It rides the **error layout** (`layout/error.html.heex`), which already solves
this exact problem for the rescued-500 path: a whole self-contained document
whose styling is inlined because it must not depend on `/assets/app.css`. A
stored page outlives the deploy it was stored in, so a reference to a digested
stylesheet would sooner or later point at a file that is no longer there — the
same reasoning, arrived at from the other direction. Borrowing it also means
one inline stylesheet to keep in step with Direction A instead of two.

Nothing here is per-member and nothing goes stale: no CSRF token, no session,
no counts. --%>
<div class="error-page">
  <h1 class="error-page__title">{gettext("No connection")}</h1>
  <p class="error-page__hint">
    {gettext(
      "vutuv needs the network for everything it shows, so there is nothing to read here until you are back online."
    )}
  </p>
  <%!-- A plain link, not history.back(): the page the member came from is the
  one that failed to load, and a reload of THIS document goes through the
  worker again and lands on the site the moment there is a network. --%>
  <p class="error-page__actions">
    <a href="/" class="button">{gettext("Try again")}</a>
  </p>
</div>
